        "Content": "Superb 3/4 bed detached residence in a wonderful situation adjacent to Castletownshend village. Located in a private development, it enjoys views over the surrounding countryside to the historic church, village, Castlehaven harbour and the coastline. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation is well laid out with modern bright interiors and generous open living space. The welcoming entrance hall leads through to the bright kitchen/dining area and further on to the living room, with high vaulted ceiling, feature fireplace and large sliding door to the rear garden. Also conveniently on the ground floor, is a large ensuite bedroom, along with the utility room & wc. \r\n\r\nOn the first floor, there are two further bedrooms, family bathroom and the mezzanine, which would be suitable for a number of uses. Ideal for a home office setup, further living space or as additional/guest accommodation. \r\n\r\nApproached over a paved driveway with parking area and attached double garage. The development is surrounded by mature trees to the rear, with the gardens being well landscaped with terrace, flower beds, rockery and shrubs. \r\n\r\nCastletownshend is a popular and unique Victorian village. The harbour is ideal for various water sports and activities and there are a number of sandy beaches within easy reach. \r\n\r\nSkibbereen is just a 10 minute drive, a bustling town with a number of excellent shops & supermarkets, bars, restaurants, a thriving country market, schools and other social amenities. Cork Airport approx. 90 minutes' drive. \r\n\r\nAccommodation:\r\n\r\nGround Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall\r\nTiled floor, understairs storage.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room: 6.2m x 3.6m. \r\nTiled floor, fitted kitchen with granite worktops, integrated appliances, tiled splash back, island unit.\r\n\r\nSitting Room: 6.2m x 4.8m. \r\nTiled floor, feature brick fireplace with stove, vaulted timber ceiling, sliding door to rear garden.\r\n\r\nWC/Utility: 2.8m x 1.8m. \r\nWC, wash hand basin & plumbed for washing machine.\r\n\r\nBedroom (1): 4.1m x 3.4m. \r\nTimber floor, built-in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nEnsuite Bathroom: 2.8m x 2.3m. \r\nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin, fitted units, bath with shower.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom (2): 4.1m x 3.8m. \r\nTimber floor, built-in wardrobes. \r\n\r\nBedroom (3): 4.1m x 2.4m. \r\nTimber floor.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom: 2.0m x 2.0m. \r\nTiled floor, WC, wash hand basin, shower.\r\n\r\nMezzanine: 3.6m x 3.5m. Timber floor.\r\n\r\nOutside: \r\nAttached double door garage\r\n\r\nServices: \r\nMains water\r\nBio-cycle unit sewerage disposal\r\n*Mains Sewerage connection pending\r\nOil fired central heating\r\n\r\nBER Details:\r\nBER: C2\r\nBER No: 105420533\r\nEPI: 188.9 kWh/m2/yr\r\n\r\nTitle: Freehold"
